---
import DashboardLayout from '../layouts/DashboardLayout.astro';
import TopBar from '../components/TopBar.astro';
import SearchModal from '../components/SearchModal.tsx';
import SkillReviewFlow from '../components/SkillReviewFlow.tsx';

export const prerender = true;

const repo = 'https://github.com/davila7/claude-code-templates';
const wf = (name: string) => `${repo}/blob/main/.github/workflows/${name}`;
---

<DashboardLayout
  title="How skills are reviewed and scanned | aitmpl.com"
  description="Every skill and plugin in the aitmpl.com catalog goes through Claude Code's validator, NVIDIA SkillSpector, a security audit and code review before it merges, and is rescanned on every catalog build."
>
  <TopBar />
  <section class="max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-10">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text-primary)] mb-2">How skills are reviewed and scanned</h1>
    <p class="text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] max-w-3xl mb-6">
      A skill reaches the catalog only through a pull request to the
      <a href={repo} class="underline hover:text-[var(--color-text-primary)]">public repository</a>, and every pull request
      runs the same checks. Pick a scenario to see what each check receives and what it passes on.
    </p>

    <SkillReviewFlow client:visible />

    <div class="prose-sec max-w-3xl mt-10 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
      <h2>The checks</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>claude plugin validate.</strong> Claude Code's own validator, run on the components a pull request changes
          and on the whole catalog every week. Errors block the merge.
          <a href={wf('component-validate.yml')}>component-validate.yml</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>NVIDIA SkillSpector.</strong> A static analyzer with 64 vulnerability patterns, run without an LLM. On a pull
          request it scans the changed skills and plugins and blocks any that score above 50 (high or critical). After merge it
          scans every component in the catalog, and the result is shown on each component page.
          <a href={wf('skill-security-scan.yml')}>skill-security-scan.yml</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Pinned external code.</strong> Skills and plugins that live in their author's repository are listed by a
          <code>source.json</code> pinned to a full commit sha with an allowed license. Upstream changes reach users only through a
          new pull request that moves the commit and passes every check again.
          <a href={wf('external-skills-outdated.yml')}>external-skills-outdated.yml</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Security audit.</strong> Five validators (structure, integrity, semantics, references, provenance) report on
          every changed Markdown component.
          <a href={wf('component-security-validation.yml')}>component-security-validation.yml</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Code review.</strong> Two review bots, cubic and greptile, comment on the diff. The PR gate does not pass while
          any review thread is unresolved, and a pull request from a fork is always merged by a maintainer.
          <a href={wf('pr-gate.yml')}>pr-gate.yml</a>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Other component types</h2>
      <p>
        Agents, commands, hooks, MCP servers, settings and mods go through the same validator and code review, and SkillSpector
        comments on them in the pull request. An MCP server's package must be pinned to an exact version, never
        <code>@latest</code>, because it starts on every Claude Code launch.
      </p>

      <h2>What this does not promise</h2>
      <p>
        Static analysis finds patterns, not intent, and it reports observations that are often expected (a security tool reads
        credentials, a hook runs commands). The scan result never changes ranking, search or recommendations, including for
        sponsored placements. Read a component's files before you install it, especially one that runs code.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <SearchModal client:idle />
</DashboardLayout>

<style is:global>
  .prose-sec h2 { color: var(--color-text-primary); font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem; }
  .prose-sec p { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
  .prose-sec ul { list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.25rem; margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
  .prose-sec li { margin: 0.5rem 0; }
  .prose-sec a { text-decoration: underline; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; }
  .prose-sec a:hover { color: var(--color-text-primary); }
  .prose-sec strong { color: var(--color-text-primary); font-weight: 600; }
  .prose-sec code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; }
</style>
